From 9f8884fb190e6973d5b7f07bc94865577eefed68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Volkhart <marius.volkhart@pkware.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 14:36:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Replace Jackson with Micronaut Serde

Swap the json/plain default converter from Jackson/Moshi to Micronaut
Serde (Jackson 3 streaming + annotations, no jackson-databind). User
payloads use the application's injected io.micronaut.serde.ObjectMapper,
wrapped in MicronautSerdePayloadConverter and supplied through
WorkflowClientOptions.Builder#setDataConverter or GlobalDataConverter.

SDK-internal protocol JSON (operation tokens, Nexus failure details,
local-activity marker metadata, search attribute values, marker scalars,
tracing headers) does not use Serde at all. It is written and read with
Jackson 3 streaming (jackson-core, a direct dependency), which needs no
mapper and no application context. A JVM-global mapper slot would break
whenever the Micronaut context that installed it stopped while another
context in the same JVM kept running workflows, because Serde resolves
serializers through its BeanContext at call time. Output is byte-identical
to the previous Jackson output; golden tests pin it.

The json/plain converter in STANDARD_PAYLOAD_CONVERTERS
(StandardJsonPayloadConverter) handles only strings, numbers, booleans,
OffsetDateTime, collections and arrays of those, string maps and
LocalActivityMarkerMetadata. Any other value throws DataConverterException
naming WorkflowClientOptions.Builder#setDataConverter, so application
types need the application's own converter. Typed search attribute unset
updates arrive as Optional and are written as json/plain null by
SearchAttributePayloadConverter.

Bumps the build to JDK 25 / Gradle 9 (Serde 3.x requires JVM 17+):
wrapper 9.6.1, --release 25, Mockito 5.23.0, logback 1.5.18 (slf4j 2.0),
Error Prone disabled on the 25 modules. Removes jackson-databind, moshi,
and okio from the runtime classpath.

Also unmasks VersionStateMachineTest, previously excluded from
:temporal-sdk:test because Moshi could not resolve AsyncWorkflowBuilder$Pair's
bare type variables (T1, T2): under Serde, Pair gets the getter-based
@Serdeable + @JsonCreator shape already used for other test-only DTOs in
this series, so DataConverter can serialize it and all 21 tests run in the
normal suite.

A library must not construct its own DI container: building a Micronaut
ApplicationContext behind a static field measured 187-223 ms and +1762
loaded classes in a non-Micronaut JVM the first time anything touched it,
and stalled the in-process test server's time-skipping "Timer task"
thread. The SDK therefore builds no mapper or context. The fork's own
test JVMs register an application-style GlobalDataConverter eagerly via a
javaagent (temporal-sdk/src/testDataConverterAgent/), since a lazy build
would pay that cost on whichever thread reaches it first. Tests that pass
enums, records and similar through a default converter use
GlobalDataConverter.get().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
